  "note": "Plan 099 bench guard: what does the rigid UV-animation lane cost on scenes that animate NOTHING? Claude, headless on the mac (DPR=2, UNCAPPED=1 - the vsync lane cannot answer a cost question), against build/original/opensa (the user's 2026-08-11 18:04 pak), 8 of the 9 ?bench=all scenes (the harness stopped at the expect count of 8; ganton-night was not reached). THIS IS A STANDING NUMBER, NOT A DELTA. The before/after pair the plan asked for could not be measured, and both attempts are recorded so nobody repeats them: (1) reverting 402a450d onto HEAD conflicts with later engine work in three places, including an unrelated drawClutter signature change - a hand-merged arm is exactly the instrument that lies; (2) a worktree at the pair itself (402a450d^ = fc0f89c8, and 402a450d) BOOTS but renders zero frames against the current pak - BOTH sides die identically on \"texture array 5 not loaded (cells must load after their arrays)\" plus an index-range overflow on a LOD render bundle (65538 indices into a 27284-byte buffer), so the incompatibility is between the 2026-08-07 engine era and the 2026-08-11 pak and has nothing to do with the UV lane. Both arms also registered 1196 road cars against today's 1219, so even a rendering old arm would not have shared the workload. A real delta needs an era-matched pak rebuild, and that pak would no longer describe today's world anyway (mod 39 deleted, procobj species floor added since). What IS established without the delta: a model with no animations allocates no uniform, writes nothing per frame and binds dynamic offset 0 on every submesh (engine.uv-anim.test.ts on the fake device), so the only always-on cost is one integer compare per rigid submesh bind. Companion numbers measured the same day on the BUILT ferris fixture: stepUvAnimation 132.2 ns/call over 2 000 000 calls with the real 261-keyframe f13d, and the observed strip cadence is 0.225 s exactly (130 steps across the 29.25 s loop), matching the authored value."